course: dictionary
lesson: 1556
title: Changeable: weather, moods and spelling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Changeable means likely to change often, so it does not stay the same for long. Look at the clues in this sentence: «The weather in Scotland is changeable: sun at breakfast, rain by lunch.» Sun, then rain, all in one day, shows that the weather keeps changing.
explain: Changeable can also describe a person's mood. «Ella's changeable mood meant she laughed one minute and sulked the next.» Here the clue is the words one minute and the next, which show her mood keeps switching.
explain: Changeable has a second meaning: able to be changed. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. If you swap in «likely to change often» and it makes sense, you have your answer. If not, try «able to be changed».
fact: Changeable means likely to change often, not staying the same.
fact: Changeable can also mean able to be changed.
fact: Weather in the UK and Ireland is often changeable: sun and rain can come in one day.
fact: «Change» becomes «changeable»: the e stays after the g, so the g still sounds soft, like a j.
fact: Two common phrases are «changeable weather» and «changeable mood».
exercise: «The weather in Ireland is very changeable, so pack a coat and a hat.» What does changeable mean here? | *Likely to change often | Always hot and dry | Very loud | Able to be changed by you
exercise: Why does «change» keep its e in «changeable»? | Because it is the plural form | To show it is a question | *To keep the g soft | To make the word longer for the page
exercise: «The changeable weather spoiled our picnic.» Find and copy the word that tells you the weather kept altering. | *changeable | picnic | our | spoiled
test: «Ella's changeable mood meant she laughed one minute and cried the next.» What does changeable mood mean? | *A mood that keeps changing | A mood that is always happy | A mood that nobody can change | A mood caused by the weather
test: Which spelling is correct for the word meaning likely to change often? | chanjable | *changeable | changable | changeabel
exam: «The rules are changeable if everyone agrees.» Which meaning of changeable fits this sentence best? | Sad and gloomy | Very noisy | *Able to be changed | Always the same
